            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ah yes sorry, it does persist with `dressing.nvim`.\r\n\r\nMy telescope setup is quite minimal:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-- more uses at: https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim#pickers\r\nrequire(\"telescope\").setup { }\r\nrequire('telescope.actions')\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_exec( \r\n[[\r\n  nnoremap <leader>ff <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').find_files()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>fg <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').git_files()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>fh <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').help_tags()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>fr <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').oldfiles()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>fc <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').commands()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>fs <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').search_history()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>fS <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').spell_suggest()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>fd <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').diagnostics()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>ft <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').treesitter()<cr>\r\n  \" nnoremap <leader>fb <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').buffers()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>gl <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').git_commits()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>gs <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').git_status()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>gb <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').git_branches()<cr>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>/ <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').live_grep()<cr>\r\n  \" -- keep for muscle memory but it should go >>>\r\n  nnoremap <leader>pf <cmd>lua require('telescope.builtin').git_files()<cr>\r\n]], false)\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nEDIT: I tried to minimize my `config` as much as I can but I still get the issue. ",
