        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thank you for checking this! 🙂\r\n\r\nIssue seems to have been resolved! Thanks!\r\n\r\nI still get a different issue when trying to load some of my sessions. Interestingly I don't have any problem with loading these specific sessions simply using `so` or from the `mini.starter` screen. But when I use `read()` for one of them I get:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nE5108: Error executing lua ...m/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/sessions.lua:194: Vim(normal):E490: No fold found\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'cmd'\r\n        ...m/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/sessions.lua:194: in function <...m/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/sessions.lua:154>\r\n        ...m/site/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/sessions.lua:371: in function 'callback'\r\n        ...er/start/dressing.nvim/lua/dressing/select/telescope.lua:58: in function 'run_replace_or_original'\r\n        ...packer/start/telescope.nvim/lua/telescope/actions/mt.lua:65: in function 'key_func'\r\n        ...k/packer/start/telescope.nvim/lua/telescope/mappings.lua:242: in function 'execute_keymap'\r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\r\n\r\nMind you I have some settings for remembering folds, custom folding etc. that I hardly remember what exactly they are. But since this doesn't happen when loading a session it is probably an indication that it is related to something extra that `mini.sessions` does inside `read()`.",
